# Portfolio — Cursor Rules

## Stack
- Vite + React
- Sanity.io for CMS (use GROQ queries, not GraphQL)
- Mux for video via @mux/mux-player-react
- sanity-plugin-mux-input in the Sanity studio
- React Router v6 for client-side routing
- Deployed on Vercel

## Project structure
- frontend/         → Vite + React app
- studio/           → Sanity Studio
- design/references/ → aesthetic reference images

## Design system rules — the most important rules in this file
- NEVER hardcode color values, font names, font sizes, spacing, or border-radius values directly in components or CSS files.
- ALWAYS use CSS custom properties from frontend/src/styles/tokens.css
- Colors: var(--color-accent)=#9e9a36 · var(--color-bg)=#fffcf4 · var(--color-ink)=#474747 · var(--color-text-primary)=#676767 · var(--color-text-muted)=#b9b9b9
- Fonts: var(--font-heading)="PT Serif" · var(--font-body)="Manrope" · var(--font-ui)="DM Mono"
- Font sizes: xs=12px · sm=16px · md=24px · lg=32px · xl=40px · 2xl=48px — use e.g. var(--size-lg), never 2rem directly
- Spacing: 2xs=4px · xs=8px · sm=16px · md=24px · lg=32px · xl=40px · 2xl=72px — use e.g. var(--space-md), never 24px directly
- Radii: use var(--radius-md)=12px, not 12px
- When in doubt, add a new token to tokens.css rather than hardcoding a one-off value.
- Case study visual hierarchy uses exactly 3 heading levels: var(--size-2xl) hero · var(--size-lg) section · var(--size-md) lead/sub

## Code conventions
- Functional components only, no class components
- No TypeScript — plain JavaScript throughout
- Custom hooks go in frontend/src/hooks/ and are prefixed with "use"
- All Sanity GROQ queries go in frontend/src/lib/queries.js
- Sanity client and image helpers go in frontend/src/lib/sanity.js
- Components go in frontend/src/components/ and are PascalCase
- Pages go in frontend/src/pages/ and are PascalCase
- Each component gets its own .css file in the same folder, using only var() references

## Sanity conventions
- Document types: caseStudy, siteSettings
- Content is modular — case studies use a contentBlocks array of typed block objects
- Block types: textBlock, imageBlock, videoBlock, statsBlock, quoteBlock
- BlockRenderer.jsx switches on block._type to render the correct component
- Never fetch data directly in a component — always use a custom hook from src/hooks/
- Sanity studio uses plain JavaScript, no TypeScript

## Mux conventions
- Videos are uploaded via the Mux plugin in Sanity Studio
- The Sanity videoBlock stores a Mux playback ID
- The frontend VideoBlock.jsx component renders <MuxPlayer playbackId={...} />
- Never embed video via a raw URL or iframe

## Environment variables
- Sanity project ID and dataset are in .env as VITE_SANITY_PROJECT_ID and VITE_SANITY_DATASET
- Access via import.meta.env.VITE_* — never hardcode project IDs in source files
- Never commit .env to git

## When building components, always
- Use token variables for all visual values
- Keep components small and single-purpose
- Use semantic HTML elements (article, section, nav, main, header, footer)
- Write CSS in a co-located .css file, not inline styles
- Make sure new components are wired into the router or a parent component before finishing

## The /design route
- frontend/src/pages/DesignSystem.jsx is a live style guide at /design
- It renders all color tokens as swatches, the full type scale, spacing blocks, and radius examples
- When making design changes, check /design first to preview before touching real pages
- Do not remove or modify DesignSystem.jsx without being asked

## Git conventions
- Commit messages use a prefix: init:, design:, feat:, fix:, content:, deploy:
- Branch names use kebab-case: feature/hero-section, fix/nav-mobile
- Commit after each meaningful unit of work, not at the end of a session
